module gunbc.type_ref_binding_authority_debt

import std.types { String }
import std.disposition { Disposition, Scaffold, SingleAuthority }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

type TypeRefDebtRosterFreezeState
  = ProvisionalUnfrozen
  | Frozen

data type_ref_debt_roster_freeze_state: TypeRefDebtRosterFreezeState = ProvisionalUnfrozen

data type_ref_census_sha: String = "89dbea7d896b3ae95195117374a8c0c9454f341e"

data type_ref_census_sha_note: String = "PIN: the hard-UnresolvedType census that closed this provisional universe was evaluated against exactly this commit (type_ref_census_sha). ContentHash 51 vs 47 was classification moving deliberate expect-red sites off the debt roster against ONE tree — not main advancing. Freeze is against this SHA (then peel re-census may advance it), never against 'today'. Disagreement is decidable: re-run compile_clean_diagnostic_histogram at the recorded SHA with GUNBC_TYPE_REF_DEBT_ADMIT=0 and compare. Same defect class as merge-admission deciding a head without the identity of the evaluated state."

data type_ref_binding_authority_debt_charter_note: String = "N1 (import-strip section 14 / swift-fox-347): pool-present type refs without binding authority refuse as UnresolvedType (same shape as absent-from-pool). The ARM REFUSES — never FloorNotYet / advisory-only class enforcement (UnlistedImportUse trap). Compile-clean, resolve typecheck gates, and gunbc run/serve share identity-grain debt / expect-red admission so incidental sites stay typed/located/counted without stopping the line — not by disabling the gate. Dissolve direction on this carrier: N2 containment grant replaces type_ref_has_binding_authority's interim import-local body; bulk type-keyed rows dissolve as a measurable event (e.g. NonEmptyStr's site set), never per-site import additions (N5: residue repair, no import lines). Honest asymmetry: values/fns bind namespace-only since #7178; types refuse-unless-imported until N2."

data type_ref_debt_freeze_sequencing_note: String = "FREEZE STATE = ProvisionalUnfrozen until witty-badger-200's peel_alias_once_for_field_access diagnostics-drop fix lands on main AND a post-merge census re-run closes the universe at a new type_ref_census_sha. PR-ready flip waits on Frozen. Meanwhile: arm, deliberate-vs-incidental classification, and debt machinery proceed. See type_ref_debt_freeze_early_receipt for the measured reason early freeze is forbidden."

data type_ref_debt_freeze_early_receipt: String = "FREEZE-EARLY RECEIPT (quiet-hawk-219 / provisional peel+arm combined census): a roster frozen before the peel fix would have refused 229 pre-existing sites as new under new-sites-refuse, each landing on an author who added nothing; measured revealed_delta unique identity = 229, retired_delta = 0 (scratch recipe df4c428366e + cherry-pick b7dfcef3465; artifacts under provisional_peel_combined/). That is the receipt the next early-freeze proposal gets pointed at. witty-badger is adding a reveals-N-retires-zero executing control to PR 7630 so retire-0 becomes repo-held rather than census-measured alone."

data type_ref_debt_provisional_combined_counts_note: String = "PROVISIONAL peel+arm combined census counts (NOT a freeze pin — do not quote as final before the post-merge pin): identity-grain unique UnresolvedType sites = 2155 (PROVISIONAL); raw SITE lines = 2998; dup_extra = 843. Peel re-resolves amplify fire multiplicity so the same TYPE×file×span can appear many times as SITE lines; the roster and revealed_delta key identity grain (2155 / revealed 229), never raw line count. Recomputing from 2998 and concluding the roster undercounts by ~40 percent is the failure mode this note exists to prevent. Standing rule until the pin: 2155 stays labeled provisional everywhere."

data type_ref_debt_site_disposition_note: String = "Per-site disposition discriminator is DELIBERATE vs INCIDENTAL — NOT path prefix. Subset = files containing unbound/refusal assertion vocabulary (word-bounded) OR section-14 RED probe fixtures. Outside the subset = incidental BY SUBSET RULE: a deliberate expect-red control must assert something about the refusal, so it would almost certainly carry the unbound/refusal vocabulary (almost certainly is the honest quantifier — not a proof). Inside the subset = execution discriminator only: DOES THE TEST/CONTROL FAIL IF THE REFERENCE BINDS? Yes → expect-red (not debt). No → incidental. Undecidable → unclassified_sites.tsv (third bucket kept alive; empty only when measured empty, never by emptying the bucket in the method)."

data type_ref_debt_roster_keying_note: String = "Rows keyed TYPE x site (file, span_start, span_end), not site alone. Ranking in provisional_debt_by_type.tsv makes N2 grant dissolution a checkable event ('this grant dissolved these N rows of type T') and ranks which single grounding buys the most. Every TSV carries census_sha as the first header field. Gate loader matches the flat TYPE\\tfile\\tstart\\tend identity."

data type_ref_roster_regenerator_choice: String = "CHOICE (b) — quiet-hawk-219 decision surface, swift-fox-347, refined: regenerate_from_census.py is an OFFLINE AUTHORING TOOL packing TWO halves that must not share one dissolve promise. NEVER invoked from CI, claim_executor, compile-clean, or any enrolled floor consumer. Checked floor artifacts are the OUTPUT rows only (SHA-pinned TSVs + type_ref_census_sha). HALF 1 PURE — census-rows-to-roster-rows regeneration (fold typed diagnostics at the pinned SHA into TYPE×site roster rows, apply already-decided classification labels): scaffolded; dissolves to a .dag fold at the next debt-contract regeneration touch (type_ref_roster_pure_regen_dissolve_trigger). HALF 2 HOST-EFFECT — deliberate/incidental execution discriminator (compile as-is vs bind-patched scratch, compare UnresolvedType counts): NOT a scaffold; it is a documented offline authoring-time measurement PROCEDURE whose typed OUTPUT (classification rows carrying bind-outcome evidence) is the artifact. No dissolve obligation. Optional only: if Wet/host_effect machinery someday makes that procedure a modeled witness, name that as type_ref_roster_host_effect_classify_optional_trigger — never a promise that peel re-census will .dag-model host-effect classification under freeze pressure."

data type_ref_roster_pure_regen_dissolve_trigger: String = "dissolve-on HALF 1 PURE: census-rows-to-roster-rows regeneration currently packed inside regenerate_from_census.py — DELETE that pure half (or the whole .py once half 2 is only a documented procedure with no remaining pure fold in the script) WHEN debt-contract machinery is next touched for regeneration (peel re-census freeze, or N2 type-keyed dissolve plumbing) AND the pure fold over pinned census diagnostics + already-decided classification labels is modeled in .dag. The pure half must not survive that touch as a silent second authority. Does NOT obligate modeling the host-effect discriminator."

data type_ref_roster_pure_regen_scaffold: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "gunbc.type_ref_binding_authority_debt",
    decl_name: "type_ref_roster_pure_regen_dissolve_trigger",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data type_ref_roster_host_effect_classify_procedure_note: String = "HALF 2 HOST-EFFECT — authoring-time measurement PROCEDURE, not a Scaffold. Procedure: for each site in the unbound/refusal-vocab subset (plus section-14 RED fixtures), ask by execution whether the control fails if the reference binds; label deliberate expect-red / incidental / unclassified; record bind-outcome evidence on the classification row. Typed OUTPUT rows are the checked artifact (expect_red_controls.tsv reasons, etc.). May keep living as offline documentation + occasional authoring re-run when peel reveals new sites. No dissolve-on. Not promised to become a .dag fold at freeze."

data type_ref_roster_host_effect_classify_optional_trigger: String = "OPTIONAL only — not a dissolve obligation: IF Wet/host_effect machinery makes the fails-if-binds discriminator a modeled witness (typed host-effect plan + read-back), THEN re-home this procedure onto that witness and retire the prose procedure note. Until that capability exists, half 2 stays a documented offline procedure. Peel re-census does not fire this."

data type_ref_binding_authority_debt_dissolve_trigger: String = "dissolve-on: (1) witty-badger-200 peel fix + re-census → update type_ref_census_sha, flip type_ref_debt_roster_freeze_state to Frozen and arm new-sites-refuse; (2) N2 containment binding authority for type positions swaps type_ref_has_binding_authority body → type-keyed roster shrinks by typed disposition to empty → delete carriers + this scaffold. Partial type-keyed shrinks are legitimate monotone progress. No import additions. At the peel re-census touch, only HALF 1 PURE roster regeneration is obligated to become a .dag fold (type_ref_roster_pure_regen_dissolve_trigger); HALF 2 host-effect classification stays the documented procedure."

data type_ref_binding_authority_debt_scaffold: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "gunbc.type_ref_binding_authority_debt",
    decl_name: "type_ref_binding_authority_debt_dissolve_trigger",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}
